;; spec:   stdlib §2.3 (Stack: Vec and List, SubVec and Queue to come), §1.2 P5, §5 T (a static-typing fact)
;; expect: reject
;; error:  no implementation of Stack for (Map i64 i64)
;; roots:  ../../lib support
;; covers: peek
;; A Map is not a stack: Clojure's (peek {1 2}) throws a ClassCastException at run time, and here the program is
;; rejected at compile time with the type that has no instance. The same holds for a Range, a Set and a str: only the
;; collections of §2.3's Stack row have the instance, and a user type adds its own (case 2561).
(ns main (:use fib.core fib.seq fib.coll))

(defun main () -> i64
  (match (peek {1 2}) ((some _) 1) (nil 0)))
